    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` following the spec, and changed no other file. Numbers are converted to `Decimal` (floats via `str()`), and `bool` inputs, non-numeric types and non-finite values are rejected. Dimensions and weight must be greater than zero, the subtotal must be zero or more, and the zone must be the `int` 1, 2 or 3. The billable weight is the larger of actual and volumetric weight (L×W×H/5000), rounded up to the next 0.5 kg. The base charge is 8.00 for up to 1 kg, plus 1.50 per further 0.5 kg, then multiplied by the zone factor (1, 1.25 or 1.6). Free shipping zeroes the base for zones 1 and 2 when the subtotal is at least 150. The 12.00 oversize surcharge applies when the longest side exceeds 120 cm and is added after both. The total is rounded to two places with `ROUND_HALF_UP` only at the end. As instructed, I did not run or test the code, so it is unverified beyond reading it against the spec.",
